' 07a Restart and lazy attach: the state of a space crosses a restart only
' through the history trie, and the first operation after the restart pays
' what a warm runtime pays.
'
' Source of the restart figure of ../verification.md (section 31). The figure
' restates design v3 section 8 (RH-1 to RH-4), the harness
' rholang/tests/reified_restart_rehydrate.rs, and the native certification of
' decision 47 (rholang/tests/support/native.rs). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order, from the top to the bottom:
'   1. Process 1 plays block 1 natively, certifies each deploy, and
'      checkpoints the spaces into the LMDB store: root R1.
'   2. Process 2 opens the store at R1. Its hot store is empty, and no Reified
'      state outlives an evaluation (F18). The first operation reads the
'      config and the records through the store of the host. A read charges
'      nothing, the same on a cold load and a warm load
'      (rule NE-2). Block 2 reaches R2, and process 2 writes the evidence
'      bytes, the event log and the cost vector of each deploy.
'   3. Process 3 certifies block 2 from its pre-state, as a validator does.
'   4. The parent plays both blocks warm and finds the same roots, cost
'      vectors, evidence bytes and event logs.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 07a-restart-lazy-attach.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 07a-restart-lazy-attach
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $rrs_relation
  LifeLineBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ParticipantBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ActorBorderColor $rrs_relation
  GroupBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
}
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Restart and lazy attach of a space, in three processes
autonumber

participant "Process 1\nblock 1" as P1 $rrs_host
database "LMDB store\nhistory trie" as STORE $rrs_storage
participant "Process 2\nrestarted node" as P2 $rrs_host
participant "Space agent\n(no cache, F18)" as AGENT $rrs_agent
participant "Store of the host" as VIEW $rrs_substrate
participant "Process 3\nvalidator" as P3 $rrs_host
participant "Parent process\nwarm run" as WARM $rrs_host

== Block 1 in process 1 ==
P1 -[$rrs_flow]> P1 : native play: create the spaces,\nstore records and waiters
P1 -[$rrs_relation]> P1 : self-certification by native replay
P1 -[$rrs_effect]> STORE : create_checkpoint(): root R1\nconfig C, counters S, records D,\nmarkers I, waiters, handle H

== Block 2 in process 2, after the restart ==
P2 -[$rrs_flow]> STORE : open the store, reset to R1
note right of P2
The hot store is empty, so no
space channel is in memory
before the first operation.
end note
P2 -[$rrs_flow]> AGENT : the first operation on a space
AGENT -[$rrs_flow]> VIEW : read the config C(sid)
VIEW -[$rrs_relation]> STORE : cold load (history read-through)
VIEW -[$rrs_relation]> VIEW : the read charges nothing (rule NE-2)
AGENT -[$rrs_flow]> VIEW : read the records and the waiters\nof the operation
AGENT -[$rrs_flow]> P2 : stage and commit, with the\nobserver calls of play (revised M-3)
P2 -[$rrs_effect]> STORE : create_checkpoint(): root R2
P2 -[$rrs_relation]> P2 : write each deploy record: roots,\ncost vector, evidence bytes, event log

== Certification of block 2 in process 3 ==
P3 -[$rrs_flow]> STORE : open the store, reset to the\npre-state root of the deploy
P3 -[$rrs_relation]> P3 : decode the evidence, check the journal,\nbind the trace to the event log
P3 -[$rrs_flow]> P3 : native replay, completeness check, export
P3 -[$rrs_relation]-> P3 : the post-state root of play and\nthe phlo usage of play (RH-1)

== Warm run in the parent process ==
WARM -[$rrs_flow]> WARM : blocks 1 and 2 in one process,\nover an in-memory store
WARM -[$rrs_relation]-> WARM : equal R1, R2, cost vectors,\nevidence bytes and event logs (RH-4)

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_host>       | host at the baseline: processes, runtime, reducer |
|<$rrs_agent>      | space agent |
|<$rrs_substrate>  | storage substrate and the store of the host |
|<$rrs_storage>    | stored state |
**Arrows**
|<$rrs_flow>       | call or return |
|<$rrs_effect>     | effect on the stored state |
|<$rrs_relation>   | read or internal step |
endlegend
@enduml
